# Compose class names with `cn`

Import `cn` from `src/lib/utils`. It wraps `clsx` and `tailwind-merge`.

Use `cn` whenever a `className` is combined with another `className` (props, variants, conditionals, or extra Tailwind strings). Do not concatenate with template strings or `+`.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<div className={`${base} ${className}`} />
<div className={"flex gap-2 " + className} />
<button className={variant === "primary" ? "bg-electric " + className : className} />

// ✅ GOOD
import { cn } from "../lib/utils";

<div className={cn("flex gap-2", className)} />
<button className={cn("rounded-md", variant === "primary" && "bg-electric", className)} />
```

A standalone literal `className="flex gap-2"` needs no `cn`.
